goto routines_intro_exit

remstart
    THE FIRST DIVE
    the very first game is a little tutorial. the wave of bubbles goes by and there is nothing there
    but the water, and one line of text: "This is a match 3 game." a light comes on down in the deep,
    the angler swims up behind it, and it cuts the line off: "Hey you! This is not JUST a match 3 game!"
    from there on, the angler says everything, in a box under the board, and it does not stop the
    game to do it. see fish_headers_guide. the confirm button skips ahead.

    THE LITTLE BOARDS
    the board has hidden rules, and the one that the little boards are about is the way that the fish
    face. every little board is the whole nine by nine board, with gaps in it where there are no fish.
    so nothing has to be hoped for:

        a row of 5      the angler says that there are lots of fish down here, and they come in as it
                        says "Look, here are some!", and that they pop in groups of 3 or more. a seahorse,
                        a seahorse, a crab, a seahorse and a goldfish. the cursor is on the crab. "Hold
                        [swap] and push [dir] to swap." once it has popped, the angler says that moving
                        the cursor costs nothing, and the row is still there to try it on. then the
                        count of moves comes in, and the multiplier, one after the other.
        the row, and    the first board with an up and a down. the only swap that does anything is the
        two more fish   one up or down, and it makes a group in the shape of an L, a few cells from the
                        cursor. the angler says, after it has popped, that fish do not need to be in
                        straight lines.
        a row of 9      two seahorses at the left, and one all the way at the right. it takes six
                        swaps to bring it home, and every one of them turns it to look left, away from
                        the other two. the angler talks about that while it is happening, not before.
                        they pop, because they do not all look the same way.
        a row of 9      the same thing, the other way around: one seahorse all the way at the left, and
                        two at the right. brought home, it looks the way that they look, so they
                        do not pop. they swim off. that is a school, and it is the last thing before the
                        whole board. if the player brings the two to the one instead, they pop, and
                        the board comes in again, with the angler telling them to slow down.

    a fish that swaps across ends up facing the way that it moved, whichever one the cursor carried.
    and every fish starts out looking right. schoolJudge leaves the first two boards alone.

    a gap is a cell with no fish in it, a value of 0. the cursor does not go into one (tutorialIsGap, from
    startLiveMove), and it is not a group (findCombos). nothing falls on a little board, because a fish
    above a gap would fall into it: a new fish comes in where the old one was, the one that the next
    board has there. a fish of a little board that the next one has too stays where it is, and the rest
    grow in. the fish are laid out by hand, in tutorialLayoutKind, and a test in fish_tests_tutorial
    plays every board.

    what the angler says depends a little on what the player does: see tutorialMissed, tutorialWatch,
    tutorialTooSoon and tutorial_pop.

    THE THINGS AROUND THE BOARD come in one at a time, and the angler swims up to each one, with an outline
    around it and everything else left alone, and says what it is. see tutorial_visit. the first pop brings
    the count of moves and then the multiplier, before the board of the L, which is the first one where they
    count. the multiplier mentions what a swap that pops nothing costs, which it only does the once. the
    rounds come with the whole board. before that, it swims back to the count of moves and says that it is
    about to reset them, and does.

    THE WHOLE BOARD
    the angler gets to finish about the school, and then the board that the game was dealt rolls out from the
    middle, a ring at a time, over the row that was there (tutorial_open_sea). it is the board that the
    game was dealt before the tutorial started, with its streams of the seed where they were, and the
    moves and the multiplier go back to how a game starts, so a seed plays the same game with the
    tutorial or without it. the bar of the round and the rounds that are left fade in with it. nothing
    goes away first: the water never shows on its own after the first line of text.

    the whole board has no room under it, so the angler crosses over it while it comes in, and talks
    from beside it from then on. it asks for info mode, the hint for it is the only hint, brighter than
    usual, and it starts to bob after a few seconds. this is the one place that waits for a key.

    the key opens info mode over the board, and the angler says what it is for, and points at the codec.
    closing it hands the game over, with the cursor, and that is the end of the tutorial
    (tutorial_goodbye). the angler stays for a little while and the player can play under it: the bar of
    the round gets an outline while it is explained, then the rounds, then that the sea can end a few
    ways, with question marks coming up out of the fish, and it swims off.

    THE FIRST UPGRADE
    the first upgrade screen of a game that had the tutorial starts with the angler alone in the dark,
    saying what upgrades are. see tutorial_first_shop, shop_greet, and fish_headers_shop.

    a piece that has not come in yet is not explained in info mode, and it does not count anything
    yet either. no moves are counted, and the multiplier does not fill, until they can be seen, and
    nothing scores until the bar can be seen. tutorialMovesOff() and tutorialScoreOff(), in
    fish_funcs, are how the rest of the game asks. the game is not saved until the tutorial is over.

    TUTORIAL_STAGE says how far along it is. it is 0 when there is no tutorial, which is nearly always,
    and then nothing here does anything.

    it happens by itself once: PREF_INTRO_SEEN remembers which INTRO_VERSION was seen, with the
    options. raising INTRO_VERSION shows a new tutorial to everyone, once. after that, the page that
    "New Game" opens has a line to ask for it again. see OPTION_GAME_INTRO.
    setting the FISH_INTRO environment variable asks for it every time, to look at it.

    the rest of the game does these things for it:
    - reset_game ends a tutorial that was going, with tutorial_end
    - starting a new game calls tutorial_prepare before the wave of bubbles, and run_first_dive_intro after it
    - handle_combos calls tutorial_pop when a move pops fish, and gives the new fish of a little board
      from tutorialNewFish
    - the main loop calls tutorial_advance, which brings in the next board once the pops have settled
    - startLiveMove asks tutorialBlocksSwap about every swap
    - judgeMultiplierSwaps calls tutorialMissed when a swap pops nothing
    - shop_greet has the words of the first upgrade screen

    THE HINTS
    this part is nothing to do with the tutorial, and it is always on. the line of key hints along the
    bottom of the game is three texts side by side: one for moving, one for swapping, and one for
    info mode. each one gives a little shake when the player does the thing that it is about, and
    the other two stay still. frame_hints lays them out and shakes them, and update_frame comes to it.

    every other screen writes its own hints on the one text that was always there, INFO_HINT_TEXT_ID.
    so the three are only shown while the game is what is being played. the screens say so with
    hintMode(), and the menu puts all of the hints away and brings them back with hintShow().
remend

setup_intro:
    ` the globals are declared in the fish headers

    ` the water goes a little darker behind the lines, so that they can be read
    reserve sprite id(INTRO_DIM_SPRITE)
    sprite INTRO_DIM_SPRITE, 0, 0, TEX_PIXEL
    set sprite offset INTRO_DIM_SPRITE, 0, 0
    size sprite INTRO_DIM_SPRITE, WORLD_WIDTH, WORLD_HEIGHT
    color sprite INTRO_DIM_SPRITE, rgb(4, 8, 24, 0)
    order sprite INTRO_DIM_SPRITE, ORDER_INTRO
    hide sprite INTRO_DIM_SPRITE

    ` at this size, the picture of a key in a line is exactly twice as big as it was drawn
    reserve text id(INTRO_TEXT_ID)
    text INTRO_TEXT_ID, WORLD_WIDTH / 2, WORLD_HEIGHT / 2, SCORE_FONT, " "
    size text max INTRO_TEXT_ID, WORLD_WIDTH - 40, 32 `a long line shrinks to fit across the screen
    set text offset INTRO_TEXT_ID, .5, .5
    color text INTRO_TEXT_ID, rgb(255, 255, 255, 0)
    ` a few orders over the dark, because the engine breaks a tie of order by id, and the dark was made later
    order text INTRO_TEXT_ID, ORDER_INTRO + 4
    enable rich text INTRO_TEXT_ID `so that a line can show a picture of a key, like {info}
    hide text INTRO_TEXT_ID

    ` the outline around the bar of the round, while the angler talks about it. see frame_guide.
    TUTORIAL_BAR_BORDER = createInfoBorder(ORDER_INTRO + 3)

    ` the question marks. a question mark is not a word, so it is the same in every language.
    for markI = 0 to TUTORIAL_MARK_COUNT - 1
        reserve text id(TUTORIAL_MARK_TEXTS(markI))
        text TUTORIAL_MARK_TEXTS(markI), 0, 0, SCORE_FONT, "?"
        size text y TUTORIAL_MARK_TEXTS(markI), 16
        set text offset TUTORIAL_MARK_TEXTS(markI), .5, .5
        color text TUTORIAL_MARK_TEXTS(markI), rgb(170, 210, 255, 255)
        order text TUTORIAL_MARK_TEXTS(markI), ORDER_INTRO + 2
        set text alpha TUTORIAL_MARK_TEXTS(markI), 0
        hide text TUTORIAL_MARK_TEXTS(markI)
        TUTORIAL_MARK_BORN(markI) = 0
    next

    ` the kinds of fish that the rows of the little boards are written in. see tutorialLayoutKind.
    TUTORIAL_KINDS(1) = TEX_PUFFER
    TUTORIAL_KINDS(2) = TEX_CATFISH
    TUTORIAL_KINDS(3) = TEX_GOLDFISH
    TUTORIAL_KINDS(4) = TEX_ANGELFISH
    TUTORIAL_KINDS(5) = TEX_CRAB
    TUTORIAL_KINDS(6) = TEX_BASS `the seahorse. see fish_routines_customart.
    TUTORIAL_KINDS(7) = TEX_WORM `the starfish

    ` the three key hints of the game. they look the same as the text that the other screens write theirs on.
    for hintI = 0 to 2
        reserve text id(HINT_PART_TEXTS(hintI))
        text HINT_PART_TEXTS(hintI), 0, WORLD_HEIGHT - 2, SCORE_FONT, " "
        order text HINT_PART_TEXTS(hintI), ORDER_HUD_TEXT
        enable rich text HINT_PART_TEXTS(hintI)
        set text offset HINT_PART_TEXTS(hintI), 0, 1
        size text y HINT_PART_TEXTS(hintI), 16
        color text HINT_PART_TEXTS(hintI), rgb(64, 128, 255, 140)
        HINT_PART_ALPHA#(hintI) = HINT_PART_SHOWN_ALPHA
        enable text drop shadow HINT_PART_TEXTS(hintI), 2, -2, rgb(0,0,0)

        reserve tween id(HINT_SHAKE_TWEENS(hintI))
        create basic tween HINT_SHAKE_TWEENS(hintI), 0, 0, 1, 0
    next
    set text loc HINT_PART_TEXTS(0), "intro.hint.move"
    set text loc HINT_PART_TEXTS(1), "intro.hint.swap"
    set text loc HINT_PART_TEXTS(2), "intro.hint.info"

    ` the jumps of the pictures of keys in the words of the tutorial. see ICON_PUNCH_TWEENS in fish_headers.
    ` the ids are the ones that frame_input_icons gives them, whatever is being played with.
    ICON_PUNCH_IDS(0) = 6 `{swap}
    ICON_PUNCH_IDS(1) = 7 `{dir}
    ICON_PUNCH_IDS(2) = 5 `{info}
    for iconI = 0 to 2
        reserve tween id(ICON_PUNCH_TWEENS(iconI))
        create basic tween ICON_PUNCH_TWEENS(iconI), 0, 0, 1, 0
    next
return


` a new game is about to start. if it is the first one, or the intro was asked for, take everything
` off of the screen, so that the wave of bubbles uncovers nothing but the water.
tutorial_prepare:
    ` the long visit is not a tutorial, but it plays on a little board. see fish_headers_puzzle.
    tutPuzzle = puzzleWanted()
    if tutPuzzle
        gosub puzzle_prepare
        return
    endif
    PUZZLE_ENV_SPENT = 1

    ` she is the one who gave the first dive. see LEAVING in fish_headers_puzzle.
    tutGone = puzzleGone()
    if tutGone
        PUZZLE_GONE_TALK = OPTION_GAME_INTRO
        OPTION_GAME_INTRO = 0
        avaGoneGame() `a few of these, and a bottle comes. see THE BOTTLE in fish_headers_ava.
        return
    endif

    tutWanted = 0
    tutSeen = get pref(PREF_INTRO_SEEN, 0)
    if tutSeen < INTRO_VERSION then tutWanted = 1
    if OPTION_GAME_INTRO then tutWanted = 1
    if is env set("FISH_INTRO") then tutWanted = 1

    ` it has to be asked for again every time
    OPTION_GAME_INTRO = 0

    if tutWanted = 0 then return
    set pref PREF_INTRO_SEEN, INTRO_VERSION
    TUTORIAL_STAGE = 1
    TUTORIAL_UPGRADE_TALK = 1 `a few words at the first upgrade screen too. see shop_greet.
    TUTORIAL_SCORE_HOLD = 0
    TUTORIAL_BOARD = 0
    TUTORIAL_STEP_DONE = 0
    TUTORIAL_VISIT = 0
    TUTORIAL_RETRY = 0
    TUTORIAL_INFO_TRIES = 0

    ` the game has been dealt its board already. it is kept for when the little boards are done, along
    ` with the way the fish face, and where the streams of the seed had got to, so that the tutorial does
    ` not change what the seed plays. see THE LITTLE BOARDS, at the top of this file.
    for tutI = 0 to CELL_COUNT - 1
        TUTORIAL_DEAL(tutI) = CELLS(tutI).value
        hide sprite CELLS(tutI).spriteId
    next
    for tutI = 0 to 399
        TUTORIAL_DEAL_FACE(tutI) = SCHOOL_FACE(tutI)
    next
    TUTORIAL_DEAL_SPAWNS = SCHOOL_SPAWNS
    for tutI = 0 to 2
        TUTORIAL_RNG(tutI * 2) = random stream state(tutI, 0)
        TUTORIAL_RNG(tutI * 2 + 1) = random stream state(tutI, 1)
    next
    hide sprite SELECTION_SPRITE
    hintShow(0)

    gosub tutorial_hide_moves
    gosub tutorial_hide_score

return


` the line of text, the angler, and then the first of the little boards. a new game comes here when
` the wave of bubbles has gone.
run_first_dive_intro:
    if PUZZLE_ON
        gosub puzzle_enter
        return
    endif
    if PUZZLE_GONE_TALK
        gosub puzzle_gone_intro
        return
    endif
    if TUTORIAL_STAGE <> 1 then return

    gosub guide_enter

    ` the fish come in as the angler says so
    guideSay(lockey$("intro.ang.fish2"))

    ` the first little board. the hints for moving and swapping are where they always are, along the
    ` bottom, and the one for info mode waits for the end.
    HINT_NO_INFO = 1
    hintShow(1)
    TUTORIAL_GROW_TO = 1
    gosub tutorial_grow
return


` a move has just popped fish on a little board. handle_combos comes here, once for every move that
` does. the first pop brings in the moves and the multiplier, with a puff of bubbles.
` the next board waits for the board to settle. see tutorial_advance.
tutorial_pop:
    if PUZZLE_ON then return
    if TUTORIAL_STEP_DONE then return
    TUTORIAL_STEP_DONE = 1
    ` what the angler says depends on how it went
    if TUTORIAL_STAGE = 2
        if TUTORIAL_SWAPS = 0
            guideSay(lockey$("intro.ang.pop1"))
        else
            guideSay(lockey$("intro.ang.pop2"))
        endif
        ` the board waits for the angler, so the row is still there to wander along
        guideThen(lockey$("intro.ang.wander"))
        TUTORIAL_VISIT = 1
    endif

    if TUTORIAL_STAGE = 3
        guideSay(lockey$("intro.tut.shape"))
        guideThen(lockey$("intro.ang.sink"))
    endif

    if TUTORIAL_STAGE = 4
        guideSay(lockey$("intro.ang.popped"))
    endif

    ` the last board is the first school. if it popped, it comes in again.
    if TUTORIAL_STAGE = 5
        if SCHOOL_COUNT > TUTORIAL_SCHOOLS_WAS
            guideSay(lockey$("intro.ang.left2"))
            tutQuick = game ms() - TUTORIAL_BOARD_MS
            if tutQuick < TUTORIAL_QUICK_MS
                guideThen(lockey$("intro.ang.fast"))
            else
                guideThen(lockey$("intro.ang.slow"))
            endif
            guideThen(lockey$("intro.ang.soon3"))
            TUTORIAL_VISIT = 3
        else
            TUTORIAL_RETRY = 1
            guideSay(lockey$("intro.ang.rushed"))
        endif
    endif
return


` the main loop comes here on every frame of the game. once a little board has popped, and the board
` has settled, the next one comes in, or the whole board does. and once info mode has been closed at
` the end of the tutorial, the game is the player's.
tutorial_advance:
    if PUZZLE_ON
        gosub puzzle_advance
        return
    endif

    ` the main loop only comes here while info mode is closed
    if TUTORIAL_STAGE = 7
        gosub tutorial_goodbye
        return
    endif

    if TUTORIAL_STAGE > 1
        if TUTORIAL_STAGE < 6
            tutorialWatch()
        endif
    endif

    if TUTORIAL_STEP_DONE = 0 then return
    if REQUEST_COMBO_CHECK then return
    if LIVE_MOVE_ACTIVE then return

    ` the board waits for the angler. the confirm button hurries it along.
    if new action down(ACT_CONFIRM)
        guideHurry()
    endif
    tutReady = guideReady()
    if tutReady = 0 then return

    if TUTORIAL_VISIT > 0
        taVisit = TUTORIAL_VISIT
        gosub tutorial_visit

        ` the count of moves, and then the multiplier, each on its own
        if taVisit = 1
            TUTORIAL_VISIT = 2
            gosub tutorial_visit
        endif
    endif

    TUTORIAL_STEP_DONE = 0
    gosub clear_queued_moves

    ` the last board comes in again, if it was not a school
    if TUTORIAL_RETRY
        TUTORIAL_RETRY = 0
        TUTORIAL_GROW_TO = 4
        gosub tutorial_grow
        return
    endif

    ` the stage is one more than the little board that was just played, so it is the next one
    if TUTORIAL_STAGE < 5
        TUTORIAL_GROW_TO = TUTORIAL_STAGE
        gosub tutorial_grow
    else
        gosub tutorial_finish
    endif
return


` bring in the little board TUTORIAL_GROW_TO. the fish that are on the board now stay where they are
` on the screen, and the new ones grow in around them, a ring at a time. the first board grows in
` from nothing. a fish that is not the one that the new board has in its spot, because the player made
` some other swap than the one that the last board was about, grows in again as the right one.
tutorial_grow:
    tgStep = TUTORIAL_GROW_TO
    tgOldSize = 0
    if TUTORIAL_BOARD then tgOldSize = CELL_COLUMN_COUNT

    ` the fish, and how they face, go with the fish, and the cells are about to be numbered again
    if tgOldSize > 0
        tgOldLast = CELL_COUNT - 1
        for tgI = 0 to tgOldLast
            EXPAND_VALUES(tgI) = CELLS(tgI).value
            TUTORIAL_FACE_KEEP(tgI) = SCHOOL_FACE(tgI)
            TUTORIAL_SHOWN_KEEP#(tgI) = SCHOOL_SHOWN#(tgI)
        next
    endif

    tgSize = tutorialLayoutSize(tgStep)
    tgShift = (tgSize - tgOldSize) / 2
    tutorialGrid(tgSize)

    tgLongest = 0
    tgLast = CELL_COUNT - 1
    for tgI = 0 to tgLast
        tgX = CELLS(tgI).coord.x
        tgY = CELLS(tgI).coord.y
        CELLS(tgI).value = tutorialLayoutKind(tgStep, tgX, tgY)
        CELLS(tgI).comboForce = 0
        CELLS(tgI).comboBlownUp = 0
        clearCellStack(tgI)
        GLOW_TURN#(tgI) = 0
        RAINBOW_FISH(tgI) = 0

        ` a gap is nothing at all, and it faces no way
        if CELLS(tgI).value = 0
            SCHOOL_FACE(tgI) = 0
            SCHOOL_SHOWN#(tgI) = 0
            hide sprite CELLS(tgI).spriteId
            hide sprite CELLS(tgI).fxSpriteId
            skip
        endif

        ` a fish that was on the last board is still there, if it is the right one
        tgKept = 0
        tgOldX = tgX - tgShift
        tgOldY = tgY - tgShift
        if tgOldSize > 0
            if tgOldX >= 0 and tgOldX < tgOldSize
                if tgOldY >= 0 and tgOldY < tgOldSize then tgKept = 1
            endif
        endif
        if tgKept
            tgOldI = tgOldX + tgOldY * tgOldSize
            if EXPAND_VALUES(tgOldI) <> CELLS(tgI).value then tgKept = 0
        endif

        if tgKept
            SCHOOL_FACE(tgI) = TUTORIAL_FACE_KEEP(tgOldI)
            SCHOOL_SHOWN#(tgI) = TUTORIAL_SHOWN_KEEP#(tgOldI)
            create basic tween CELLS(tgI).scaleWaveTweenId, 1, 1, 1, 0
        else
            schoolNewFish(tgI)
            tutorialFaceRight(tgI)

            ` a new fish grows in with the ring around the board that it is on, going out from the middle.
            ` the rings go one after the other, and the fish of a ring follow each other around it a little.
            tgRingX = tgX - tgSize / 2
            if tgRingX < 0 then tgRingX = 0 - tgRingX
            tgRingY = tgY - tgSize / 2
            if tgRingY < 0 then tgRingY = 0 - tgRingY
            tgRing = tgRingX
            if tgRingY > tgRing then tgRing = tgRingY
            tgDelay = tgRing * TUTORIAL_GROW_STAGGER + (tgX + tgY) * 12
            if tgDelay > tgLongest then tgLongest = tgDelay
            create basic tween CELLS(tgI).scaleWaveTweenId, 0, 1, TUTORIAL_GROW_MS, tgDelay
            size sprite CELLS(tgI).spriteId, 0, 0
            spawnBubbles(getCellX(tgX), getCellY(tgY), CELL_SIZE / 4, 3, tgDelay + 100, FISH_COLORS(getFishColorIndex(CELLS(tgI).value)))
        endif

        updateCell(CELLS(tgI))
        set sprite alpha CELLS(tgI).spriteId, 255
        show sprite CELLS(tgI).spriteId
        hide sprite CELLS(tgI).fxSpriteId
    next

    ` the cursor stays on the fish that it was on. on the first board, it starts in the middle, on the crab.
    if tgOldSize > 0
        SELECTION_POS.x = SELECTION_POS.x + tgShift
        SELECTION_POS.y = SELECTION_POS.y + tgShift
    else
        SELECTION_POS.x = tgSize / 2
        SELECTION_POS.y = tgSize / 2
    endif
    ` the row that it was off of has gone, so it comes back to the row of the board
    if SELECTION_POS.y <> 4
        tgCursorCell = SELECTION_POS.x + SELECTION_POS.y * tgSize
        if CELLS(tgCursorCell).value = 0 then SELECTION_POS.y = 4
    endif
    scale sprite SELECTION_SPRITE, CELL_SIZE, CELL_SIZE
    gosub update_selection_position
    cursorArrive(tgLongest + TUTORIAL_GROW_MS) `once the last fish has grown in. see fish_headers_cursorshow.

    TUTORIAL_BOARD = 1
    TUTORIAL_STEP_DONE = 0
    TUTORIAL_STAGE = tgStep + 1

    ` the fish grow in while the game waits. the frame goes on being drawn underneath.
    TUTORIAL_WAIT_UNTIL = game ms() + tgLongest + TUTORIAL_GROW_MS
    gosub tutorial_wait

    TUTORIAL_SWAPS = 0
    TUTORIAL_WAIT_SAID = 0
    TUTORIAL_SCHOOLS_WAS = SCHOOL_COUNT
    TUTORIAL_BOARD_MS = game ms()
    TUTORIAL_IDLE_MS = game ms()

    ` and the angler says what the board is about. the player can get on with it while it talks. once
    ` a board has been swapped on, tutorialMissed has it talk about what is happening.
    if tgStep = 1
        guideThen(lockey$("intro.tut.swap"))
    endif
    if tgStep = 2
        guideSay(lockey$("intro.ang.updown"))
    endif
    if tgStep = 3
        guideSay(lockey$("intro.ang.carry"))
    endif
    if tgStep = 4
        if ANGLER_SPEAKING + GUIDE_QUEUED = 0
            guideSay(lockey$("intro.ang.again"))
        endif
    endif
return


` the angler swims up to one thing around the board, and says what it is, and swims back. what comes
` next waits for it. see THE THINGS AROUND THE BOARD at the top of this file. TUTORIAL_VISIT says which:
` 1 the count of moves, 2 the multiplier, 3 the count of moves again, to reset it, and 4 the rounds.
tutorial_visit:
    tvWhich = TUTORIAL_VISIT
    TUTORIAL_VISIT = 0

    tvBlob = INFO_INDEX_MOVE_COUNT
    if tvWhich = 2 then tvBlob = INFO_INDEX_MULTIPLIER
    if tvWhich = 4 then tvBlob = INFO_INDEX_ROUNDS
    if tvWhich = 1
        gosub tutorial_show_count
    endif
    if tvWhich = 2
        gosub tutorial_show_mult
        resetMultiplier()
        refreshMultiplier(0)
    endif
    if tvWhich < 3
        tvBubbleX = INFOS(tvBlob).topLeft.x + INFOS(tvBlob).size.x / 2
        tvBubbleY = INFOS(tvBlob).topLeft.y + INFOS(tvBlob).size.y / 2
        spawnBubbles(tvBubbleX, tvBubbleY, 22, 14, 0, rgb(255, 255, 255))
    endif

    guideVisit(tvBlob)
    while is tween done(GUIDE_VISIT_TWEEN_ID) < 1
        gosub update_frame
        sync
    endwhile

    if tvWhich = 1
        guideSay(lockey$("intro.ang.count"))
    endif
    if tvWhich = 2
        guideSay(lockey$("intro.ang.mult"))
        guideThen(lockey$("intro.ang.miss"))
        wiggleMultiplierBar()
    endif
    if tvWhich = 3
        guideSay(lockey$("intro.ang.reset"))
    endif
    if tvWhich = 4
        anglerSay(loc$("intro.ang.rounds2", "rounds", GAME_ROUND_CAP))
    endif

    tvReady = 0
    while tvReady = 0
        gosub frame_input_icons
        tvHurry = new action down(ACT_CONFIRM)
        tvClick = mouseClickAnywhere()
        if tvClick then tvHurry = 1
        if tvHurry
            guideHurry()
        endif
        tvReady = guideReady()
        gosub update_frame
        sync
    endwhile

    ` the moves were practice, and they go, where the player can see it
    if tvWhich = 3
        CURRENT_MOVE_COUNT = 0
        set text MOVE_COUNT_TEXT_ID, "0"
        resetMultiplier()
        refreshMultiplier(150)
        tvBubbleX = INFOS(tvBlob).topLeft.x + INFOS(tvBlob).size.x / 2
        tvBubbleY = INFOS(tvBlob).topLeft.y + INFOS(tvBlob).size.y / 2
        spawnBubbles(tvBubbleX, tvBubbleY, 26, 18, 0, rgb(255, 222, 96))
        TUTORIAL_WAIT_UNTIL = game ms() + 900
        gosub tutorial_wait
    endif

    guideVisitEnd()
    while is tween done(GUIDE_VISIT_TWEEN_ID) < 1
        gosub update_frame
        sync
    endwhile
return


` THE FIRST UPGRADE. before there are any cards, the dark comes down, and there is only the angler, who
` says what the upgrades are, in the broadest way. handle_ability_selection comes here, and the upgrade
` screen comes up behind it. the confirm button hurries it along.
tutorial_first_shop:
    hintShow(0)
    color sprite INTRO_DIM_SPRITE, rgb(2, 6, 16, 0)
    show sprite INTRO_DIM_SPRITE
    guideShow()
    create basic tween GUIDE_GLOW_TWEEN_ID, 0, 1, GUIDE_LIGHT_MS, 0
    create basic tween ANGLER_SWIM_TWEEN_ID, 0, 1, GUIDE_ENTER_MS, 0
    tfsStart = game ms()
    tfsTalked = 0
    tfsDone = 0
    while tfsDone = 0
        tfsAge# = game ms() - tfsStart
        tfsDim# = tfsAge# / 900
        if tfsDim# > 1 then tfsDim# = 1
        color sprite INTRO_DIM_SPRITE, rgb(2, 6, 16, 238 * tfsDim#)

        if tfsTalked = 0
            if tfsAge# >= GUIDE_ENTER_MS
                tfsTalked = 1
                create basic tween GUIDE_BOX_TWEEN_ID, 0, 1, 250, 0
                guideSay(lockey$("intro.line.round1"))
                guideThen(lockey$("intro.line.goodjob"))
                guideThen(lockey$("intro.ang.passive"))
                guideThen(lockey$("intro.ang.custom"))
                guideThen(lockey$("intro.line.upgrade"))
            endif
        else
            gosub frame_input_icons
            tfsHurry = new action down(ACT_CONFIRM)
            tfsClick = mouseClickAnywhere()
            if tfsClick then tfsHurry = 1
            if tfsHurry
                guideHurry()
            endif
            tfsDone = guideReady()
        endif

        gosub update_frame
        sync
    endwhile

    guideLeave()
    while GUIDE_ON
        gosub update_frame
        sync
    endwhile
    hintShow(1)
return


` draw frames until TUTORIAL_WAIT_UNTIL, while something of the tutorial plays out
tutorial_wait:
    while game ms() < TUTORIAL_WAIT_UNTIL
        gosub update_frame
        sync
    endwhile
return


` the board that the game was dealt rolls out from the middle, a ring at a time, over the little board.
` a fish that is there goes first, and the new one grows in where it was. the swaps of the little boards
` are not part of the game, so the streams of the seed go back to where they were, and the moves and the
` multiplier go back to how a game starts. the bar of the round and the rounds that are left fade in
` with it. the angler gets out of the way.
tutorial_open_sea:
    TUTORIAL_BOARD = 0
    hide sprite SELECTION_SPRITE
    guideAside()

    HUD_KEEP_BAR# = 0
    gosub tutorial_show_score
    applyHudFade()

    tosStart = game ms()
    tosLast = CELL_COUNT - 1
    tosLongest = 0
    for tosI = 0 to tosLast
        tosRingX = CELLS(tosI).coord.x - CELL_COLUMN_COUNT / 2
        if tosRingX < 0 then tosRingX = 0 - tosRingX
        tosRingY = CELLS(tosI).coord.y - CELL_ROW_COUNT / 2
        if tosRingY < 0 then tosRingY = 0 - tosRingY
        tosRing = tosRingX
        if tosRingY > tosRing then tosRing = tosRingY
        tosDelay = tosRing * TUTORIAL_SEA_STAGGER + (CELLS(tosI).coord.x + CELLS(tosI).coord.y) * 8
        if tosDelay > tosLongest then tosLongest = tosDelay
        if CELLS(tosI).value > 0
            tosFrom# = tweenVal(CELLS(tosI).scaleWaveTweenId)
            create basic tween CELLS(tosI).scaleWaveTweenId, tosFrom#, 0, TUTORIAL_GROW_MS, tosDelay
        endif
        TUTORIAL_TURN_AT(tosI) = tosStart + tosDelay + TUTORIAL_GROW_MS
    next

    tosEnd = tosStart + tosLongest + TUTORIAL_GROW_MS + TUTORIAL_FISH_GROW
    tosSpan# = tosEnd - tosStart
    while game ms() < tosEnd
        tosNow = game ms()
        for tosI = 0 to tosLast
            if TUTORIAL_TURN_AT(tosI) > 0
                if tosNow >= TUTORIAL_TURN_AT(tosI)
                    TUTORIAL_TURN_AT(tosI) = 0
                    tutorialDealCell(tosI)
                endif
            endif
        next
        tosAge# = tosNow - tosStart
        HUD_KEEP_BAR# = tosAge# / tosSpan#
        if HUD_KEEP_BAR# > 1 then HUD_KEEP_BAR# = 1
        gosub update_frame
        applyHudFade()
        sync
    endwhile
    HUD_KEEP_BAR# = 1
    applyHudFade()

    tutorialDealDone()
    SELECTION_POS.x = CELL_COLUMN_COUNT / 2
    SELECTION_POS.y = CELL_ROW_COUNT / 2
    scale sprite SELECTION_SPRITE, CELL_SIZE, CELL_SIZE
    gosub update_selection_position
    set text MOVE_COUNT_TEXT_ID, "0"
return


` the third little board has swum off. the whole board comes in, and the angler asks for info mode. the
` key opens it, over that same board.
tutorial_finish:
    gosub tutorial_open_sea
    guideBeside()
    TUTORIAL_VISIT = 4
    gosub tutorial_visit

    ` the angler says the line about info mode, and the hint for it is on its own, where it always is.
    ` frame_hints makes it bob after a while.
    TUTORIAL_STAGE = 6
    HINT_NO_INFO = 0
    HINT_ONLY_INFO = 1
    hintShow(1)
    TUTORIAL_KEY_MS = game ms()
    guideSay(lockey$("intro.ang.peek2"))
    guideThen(lockey$("intro.line.info"))

    tfEntered = 0
    while tfEntered = 0
        ` the main loop is not running, so this keeps the picture of the key right. it is a
        ` picture of a button if the player picks up a controller.
        gosub frame_input_icons
        if new action down(ACT_INFO) then tfEntered = 1
        gosub update_frame
        sync
    endwhile

    TUTORIAL_KEY_MS = 0
    HINT_ONLY_INFO = 0
    hintShow(1)

    ` info mode opens over the board, which is what the player asked for. the hint to close it again
    ` starts to bob, if it is left open. when it is closed, tutorial_advance comes to tutorial_goodbye.
    TUTORIAL_STAGE = 7
    TUTORIAL_INFO_MS = game ms()
    gosub info_open
    guideSay(lockey$("intro.ang.look"))
    guideThen(lockey$("intro.ang.codec2"))
return


` info mode has been closed, and the game is the player's. the tutorial is over, and the angler stays
` for a little while, and talks while the player plays. see frame_guide for the outline around the bar,
` and the question marks.
tutorial_goodbye:
    TUTORIAL_STAGE = 0
    cursorArrive(0)
    tgbX = SCORE_POS.x - 6
    tgbY = SCORE_POS.y - 19
    tgbW = SCORE_SIZE.x + 12
    layoutInfoBorder(TUTORIAL_BAR_BORDER, tgbX, tgbY, tgbW, 39)
    guideSay(lockey$("intro.tut.bar"))
    guideThen(lockey$("intro.tut.bar.sub"))
    guideThen(lockey$("intro.line.nolose"))
    guideThen(lockey$("intro.ang.end2"))
    guideThen(lockey$("intro.ang.secrets"))
    guideThen(lockey$("intro.ang.trust"))
    GUIDE_END_TALK = 1
return


` put back everything that a tutorial took away. reset_game comes here, so that a game that is
` started while a tutorial is still going has all of its pieces.
tutorial_end:
    TUTORIAL_SCORE_HOLD = 0
    TUTORIAL_INFO_MS = 0
    TUTORIAL_UPGRADE_TALK = 0
    guideOff()
    if GUIDE_MARKS_UNTIL > 0
        GUIDE_MARKS_UNTIL = 0
        tutorialMarksClear()
    endif
    if PUZZLE_ON
        gosub puzzle_end
    endif
    if TUTORIAL_STAGE = 0 then return
    TUTORIAL_STAGE = 0
    TUTORIAL_BOARD = 0
    TUTORIAL_STEP_DONE = 0

    TUTORIAL_KEY_MS = 0
    HINT_ONLY_INFO = 0
    HINT_NO_INFO = 0
    hide sprite INTRO_DIM_SPRITE
    hide text INTRO_TEXT_ID
    HUD_KEEP# = 1

    ` a little board is put away. reset_game deals the whole board again.
    resizeGrid(GRID_START_COUNT, GRID_START_COUNT)
    scale sprite SELECTION_SPRITE, CELL_SIZE, CELL_SIZE

    for tutI = 0 to CELL_COUNT - 1
        create basic tween CELLS(tutI).scaleWaveTweenId, 1, 1, 1, 0
        show sprite CELLS(tutI).spriteId
    next
    cursorArriveEnd(0)
    show sprite SELECTION_SPRITE
    hintShow(1)

    gosub tutorial_show_moves
    gosub tutorial_show_score
    applyHudFade()
return


` the count of moves, and the multiplier, on the left of the board. info mode does not explain them while they are away.
tutorial_hide_moves:
    hide text MOVES_LABEL_TEXT_ID
    hide text MOVE_COUNT_TEXT_ID
    hide text MULT_LABEL_TEXT_ID
    hide text MULT_TEXT_ID
    hide text MULT_NUM_TEXT_ID
    hide sprite MULT_BAR_BACK_SPRITE
    hide sprite MULT_BAR_FILL_SPRITE
    hide sprite MULT_BAR_CHARGE_SPRITE
    hide sprite MULT_BAR_GLINT_SPRITE
    setInfoBlobEnabled(INFO_INDEX_MOVE_COUNT, 0)
    setInfoBlobEnabled(INFO_INDEX_MULTIPLIER, 0)
return

tutorial_show_moves:
    gosub tutorial_show_count
    gosub tutorial_show_mult
return

tutorial_show_count:
    show text MOVES_LABEL_TEXT_ID
    show text MOVE_COUNT_TEXT_ID
    setInfoBlobEnabled(INFO_INDEX_MOVE_COUNT, 1)
return

tutorial_show_mult:
    show text MULT_LABEL_TEXT_ID
    show text MULT_TEXT_ID
    show text MULT_NUM_TEXT_ID
    show sprite MULT_BAR_BACK_SPRITE
    show sprite MULT_BAR_FILL_SPRITE
    show sprite MULT_BAR_CHARGE_SPRITE
    show sprite MULT_BAR_GLINT_SPRITE
    setInfoBlobEnabled(INFO_INDEX_MULTIPLIER, 1)
return


` the bar of the round's progress, above the board, and the rounds that are left, on the right of it
tutorial_hide_score:
    hide sprite SCORE_BAR.backgroundSpriteId
    hide sprite SCORE_BAR.foregroundSpriteId
    for introOverI = 0 to CHARGE_SLICE_COUNT - 1
        hide sprite CHARGE_OVER_SPRITES(introOverI)
    next
    for introChargeI = 0 to CHARGE_SLICE_COUNT - 1
        hide sprite CHARGE_SPRITES(introChargeI)
    next
    hide text CHARGE_TEXT_ID
    hide text SCORE_BAR.textNumId
    hide text SCORE_BAR.textTitleId
    hide text ROUNDS_LABEL_TEXT_ID
    hide text ROUND_COUNT_TEXT_ID
    setInfoBlobEnabled(INFO_INDEX_SCORE_BAR, 0)
    setInfoBlobEnabled(INFO_INDEX_ROUNDS, 0)
return

tutorial_show_score:
    show sprite SCORE_BAR.backgroundSpriteId
    show sprite SCORE_BAR.foregroundSpriteId
    for introOverI = 0 to CHARGE_SLICE_COUNT - 1
        show sprite CHARGE_OVER_SPRITES(introOverI)
    next
    for introChargeI = 0 to CHARGE_SLICE_COUNT - 1
        show sprite CHARGE_SPRITES(introChargeI)
    next
    show text CHARGE_TEXT_ID
    show text SCORE_BAR.textNumId
    show text SCORE_BAR.textTitleId
    show text ROUNDS_LABEL_TEXT_ID
    show text ROUND_COUNT_TEXT_ID
    setInfoBlobEnabled(INFO_INDEX_SCORE_BAR, 1)
    setInfoBlobEnabled(INFO_INDEX_ROUNDS, 1)
return


` lay out the three key hints of the game, and shake the one that is about what the player just did.
` update_frame comes here on every frame of the game. see THE HINTS, at the top of this file.
frame_hints:

    ` a direction on its own is a move, and a direction while the swap button is held is a swap
    hintDir = 0
    if new action down(ACT_LEFT) then hintDir = 1
    if new action down(ACT_RIGHT) then hintDir = 1
    if new action down(ACT_UP) then hintDir = 1
    if new action down(ACT_DOWN) then hintDir = 1
    if hintDir
        if action down(ACT_SWAP)
            create basic tween HINT_SHAKE_TWEENS(1), 1, 0, HINT_SHAKE_MS, 0
        else
            create basic tween HINT_SHAKE_TWEENS(0), 1, 0, HINT_SHAKE_MS, 0
        endif
    endif
    if new action down(ACT_INFO)
        create basic tween HINT_SHAKE_TWEENS(2), 1, 0, HINT_SHAKE_MS, 0
    endif

    ` the pictures of keys in the words of the tutorial jump when their key is pressed, the swap
    ` button on its own, and the direction whether or not the swap button is held
    hintIconHit0 = new action down(ACT_SWAP)
    hintIconHit2 = new action down(ACT_INFO)
    if hintIconHit0
        iconPunch(0)
    endif
    if hintDir
        iconPunch(1)
    endif
    if hintIconHit2
        iconPunch(2)
    endif
    for hintIconI = 0 to 2
        hintIconScale# = 1 + tweenVal(ICON_PUNCH_TWEENS(hintIconI)) * ICON_PUNCH_SIZE#
        set text icon scale INTRO_TEXT_ID, ICON_PUNCH_IDS(hintIconI), hintIconScale#
        set text icon scale ANGLER_SAY_TEXT_ID, ICON_PUNCH_IDS(hintIconI), hintIconScale#
    next

    ` they sit in a row, in the middle of the screen. the pictures of the keys are not the same width
    ` as the pictures of the controller buttons, so the row is measured again on every frame.
    hintWidth0# = get text size x(HINT_PART_TEXTS(0))
    hintWidth1# = get text size x(HINT_PART_TEXTS(1))
    hintWidth2# = get text size x(HINT_PART_TEXTS(2))
    hintRow# = hintWidth0# + hintWidth1# + hintWidth2# + HINT_PART_GAP * 2
    hintHalf# = hintRow# / 2
    hintX# = WORLD_WIDTH / 2 - hintHalf#

    ` a shake dies away, and the hint ends up back where it started
    hintWave# = sin(game ms() * .07) * HINT_SHAKE_SIZE#

    set text position HINT_PART_TEXTS(0), hintX# + hintWave# * tweenVal(HINT_SHAKE_TWEENS(0)), WORLD_HEIGHT - 2
    hintX# = hintX# + hintWidth0# + HINT_PART_GAP
    set text position HINT_PART_TEXTS(1), hintX# + hintWave# * tweenVal(HINT_SHAKE_TWEENS(1)), WORLD_HEIGHT - 2
    hintX# = hintX# + hintWidth1# + HINT_PART_GAP

    ` in the very first game, the hint for info mode is on its own to start with. if the player has
    ` not pressed the key after a while, the hint bobs: up a little and back down to where it sits,
    ` gently. it starts from where it sits, so it does not jump.
    hintKeyBob = 0
    if TUTORIAL_KEY_MS > 0
        hintKeyWait# = game ms() - TUTORIAL_KEY_MS
        if hintKeyWait# > TUTORIAL_NUDGE_MS
            hintKeyAge# = hintKeyWait# - TUTORIAL_NUDGE_MS
            hintKeyBob = (cos(hintKeyAge# * TUTORIAL_NUDGE_SPEED#) - 1) * TUTORIAL_NUDGE_SIZE
        endif
    endif

    ` a - b + c comes out as a - (b + c), so the subtraction goes last
    set text position HINT_PART_TEXTS(2), hintX# + hintWave# * tweenVal(HINT_SHAKE_TWEENS(2)), WORLD_HEIGHT + hintKeyBob - 2

    ` in the very first game, info mode opened by itself, and the only hint is the one to close it.
    ` if it has been left open for a while, that hint bobs the same way, to ask for the key.
    if TUTORIAL_INFO_MS > 0
        hintBob = 0
        if INFO_MODE = 0
            TUTORIAL_INFO_MS = 0
        else
            hintWaited# = game ms() - TUTORIAL_INFO_MS
            if hintWaited# > TUTORIAL_INFO_NUDGE_MS
                hintBobAge# = hintWaited# - TUTORIAL_INFO_NUDGE_MS
                hintBob = (cos(hintBobAge# * TUTORIAL_NUDGE_SPEED#) - 1) * TUTORIAL_NUDGE_SIZE
            endif
        endif

        ` a - b + c comes out as a - (b + c), so the subtraction goes last
        set text position INFO_HINT_TEXT_ID, WORLD_WIDTH / 2, WORLD_HEIGHT + hintBob - 2
    endif
return


routines_intro_exit:


` say if the hints along the bottom are the three of the game (1), or if some other screen has
` written its own hints on INFO_HINT_TEXT_ID (0)
function hintMode(isGame)
    HINT_GAME_ON = isGame
    applyHints()
endfunction


` make a picture of a key in the words of the tutorial jump: 0 is {swap}, 1 is {dir}, and 2 is {info}.
` it grows and comes back, the same way the cursor punches. see ICON_PUNCH_TWEENS in fish_headers.
function iconPunch(punchWhich)
    create basic tween ICON_PUNCH_TWEENS(punchWhich), 0, 1, ICON_PUNCH_MS, 0
    set tween type ICON_PUNCH_TWEENS(punchWhich), 1
endfunction


` put all of the hints away (0), or bring them back (1)
function hintShow(isVisible)
    HINT_VISIBLE = isVisible
    if isVisible
        show text INFO_HINT_TEXT_ID
    else
        hide text INFO_HINT_TEXT_ID
    endif
    applyHints()
endfunction


` the three key hints of the game are only there while the hints are showing, and the game is what
` they are for. this only decides where each one is headed. stepHintFade() takes it there.
function applyHints()
    for hintI = 0 to 2
        show text HINT_PART_TEXTS(hintI) `one that has faded all the way out is hidden again by stepHintFade()
    next
endfunction


` how see-through one of the three key hints of the game should be right now, out of 255
function hintPartWant(part)
    want = 0
    if HINT_VISIBLE
        if HINT_GAME_ON then want = HINT_PART_SHOWN_ALPHA
    endif

    ` the hint for info mode on its own, at the start of the very first game. it is bright, to be seen.
    if HINT_ONLY_INFO
        if want > 0
            want = 0
            if part = 2 then want = 255
        endif
    endif

    ` and while the little boards are played, it is the one that is left out
    if HINT_NO_INFO
        if part = 2 then want = 0
    endif
endfunction want


` fade the three key hints of the game toward where they should be. updateSeabed() calls this, which
` is called wherever frames are being drawn, so the hints fade under the menus and the upgrade screen too.
` it works out how much time has gone by on its own, so calling it twice on a frame does no harm.
function stepHintFade()
    fadeNow = game ms()
    fadeElapsed# = fadeNow - HINT_FADE_LAST_MS
    HINT_FADE_LAST_MS = fadeNow
    if fadeElapsed# > 50 then fadeElapsed# = 50
    if fadeElapsed# <= 0 then exitfunction

    ` the texts are not made until setup_intro has run
    if HINT_PART_TEXTS(0) = 0 then exitfunction

    fadeStep# = (fadeElapsed# * 255) / HINT_FADE_MS#

    for hintI = 0 to 2
        want# = hintPartWant(hintI)
        alpha# = HINT_PART_ALPHA#(hintI)
        if alpha# < want#
            alpha# = alpha# + fadeStep#
            if alpha# > want# then alpha# = want#
        endif
        if alpha# > want#
            alpha# = alpha# - fadeStep#
            if alpha# < want# then alpha# = want#
        endif
        HINT_PART_ALPHA#(hintI) = alpha#

        set text alpha HINT_PART_TEXTS(hintI), alpha#
        if alpha# <= 0
            hide text HINT_PART_TEXTS(hintI)
        else
            show text HINT_PART_TEXTS(hintI)
        endif
    next
endfunction


` THE LITTLE BOARDS. see the top of this file.

` how many cells there are across a little board, and down it. 0 for one that there is not. they
` are all the whole board, with gaps in it.
function tutorialLayoutSize(tlsStep)
    tlsSize = 0
    if tlsStep >= 1
        if tlsStep <= 4 then tlsSize = GRID_START_COUNT
    endif
endfunction tlsSize


` 1 when this cell is a gap in a little board. see THE LITTLE BOARDS, at the top of this file.
function tutorialIsGap(tigCell)
    tigIs = 0
    if TUTORIAL_BOARD
        if CELLS(tigCell).value = 0 then tigIs = 1
    endif
endfunction tigIs


` every fish of a little board starts out looking right, so that the way that a fish turns can be seen
function tutorialFaceRight(tfrCell)
    SCHOOL_FACE(tfrCell) = 1
    tfrArt = schoolArtFace(CELLS(tfrCell).value)
    SCHOOL_SHOWN#(tfrCell) = 0
    if tfrArt <> 0
        if tfrArt <> 1 then SCHOOL_SHOWN#(tfrCell) = 1
    endif
endfunction


` handle_combos draws every cell again after a pop, and a gap has nothing to show
function tutorialHideGaps()
    thgLast = CELL_COUNT - 1
    for thgI = 0 to thgLast
        if CELLS(thgI).value = 0
            hide sprite CELLS(thgI).spriteId
        endif
    next
endfunction


` the kind of fish that a little board has in a cell. every row is a number, one digit for every cell,
` and a digit is a kind of fish from TUTORIAL_KINDS:
`     1 puffer, 2 catfish, 3 goldfish, 4 angelfish, 5 crab, 6 seahorse, 7 starfish
` the letters next to the rows say the same: P F G A C S W, and a dot for a gap. a row that is not
` here is all gaps, and a row that starts with gaps starts with zeros, which a number leaves off.
` a board has no group of three to start with, and only the swap that the board is about makes one.
` the fish that drop in after its pop are the ones that the next board has there.
` fish_tests_tutorial checks all of that.
function tutorialLayoutKind(tlkStep, tlkX, tlkY)
    tlkRow = 0

    ` the seahorses: swap the crab with the seahorse to the right of it. the cursor starts on the crab.
    if tlkStep = 1
        if tlkY = 4 then tlkRow = 6656300 `. . S S C S G . .
    endif

    ` swap the puffer with the seahorse under it, and the three of them make an L
    if tlkStep = 2
        if tlkY = 3 then tlkRow = 6000000 `. . S . . . . . .
        if tlkY = 4 then tlkRow = 326125372 `G F S P F C G W F
        if tlkY = 5 then tlkRow = 600000 `. . . S . . . . .
    endif

    ` the seahorse at the end comes all the way to the left, and looks away from the other two
    if tlkStep = 3
        if tlkY = 4 then tlkRow = 664125376 `S S A P F C G W S
    endif

    ` the seahorse at the start comes all the way to the right, and looks the way that the other two do
    if tlkStep = 4
        if tlkY = 4 then tlkRow = 625413766 `S F C A P G W S S
    endif

    ` the digit of the cell. the first cell of a row is the first digit.
    tlkPlace = tutorialLayoutSize(tlkStep) - 1
    tlkPlace = tlkPlace - tlkX
    while tlkPlace > 0
        tlkRow = tlkRow / 10
        tlkPlace = tlkPlace - 1
    endwhile
    tlkDigit = tlkRow mod 10

    tlkKind = 0
    if tlkDigit > 0 then tlkKind = TUTORIAL_KINDS(tlkDigit)
endfunction tlkKind


` where the fish that a little board is about is, after `tscSwaps` swaps of bringing it home
function tutorialSwapCell(tscStep, tscSwaps)
    tscX = 5 - tscSwaps
    tscY = 4
    if tscStep = 2
        tscX = 3
        tscY = 5 - tscSwaps
    endif
    if tscStep = 3 then tscX = 8 - tscSwaps
    if tscStep = 4 then tscX = tscSwaps
    tscCell = tscX + tscY * tutorialLayoutSize(tscStep)
endfunction tscCell


` how many swaps it takes to bring that fish home
function tutorialCarrySwaps(tcsStep)
    tcsSwaps = 6
    if tcsStep < 3 then tcsSwaps = 1
endfunction tcsSwaps


` make the board a little board, `tgSize` cells across and down. resizeGrid would make its cells big,
` to fill the square of the screen that the board has. a little board keeps the cells the size that
` they are on the board that a game starts with instead, so that it sits in the middle of where that
` board will be, and every cell of it is in the spot of a cell of that board.
function tutorialGrid(tgSize)
    resizeGrid(tgSize, tgSize)
    CELL_SIZE = CELL_START_SIZE
    CELL_ART_SIZE = CELL_START_ART_SIZE

    ` a - b + c comes out as a - (b + c), so the subtraction goes last
    GRID_POS.x = GRID_CENTER.x + CELL_SIZE / 2 - (tgSize * CELL_SIZE) / 2
    GRID_POS.y = GRID_CENTER.y + CELL_SIZE / 2 - (tgSize * CELL_SIZE) / 2

    ` the smoke of a pop is the size that it is on that board too
    tgLast = CELL_MAX_COUNT - 1
    for tgFx = 0 to tgLast
        scale sprite CELLS(tgFx).fxSpriteId, 1, 1
    next

    ` info mode explains the board, wherever the board is now
    coralPlaceInfo()
endfunction


` the kind of the new fish that drops into a cell of a little board, after a pop. it is the fish that
` the next board has in that spot. the last board makes way for the whole board, so any fish that does
` not pop will do there. this does not roll the streams of the seed.
function tutorialNewFish(tnfCell)
    if PUZZLE_ON then exitfunction 0 `nothing comes back. see fish_headers_puzzle.
    tnfNext = TUTORIAL_STAGE `one more than the little board that is being played
    if TUTORIAL_RETRY then tnfNext = 4
    tnfNextSize = tutorialLayoutSize(tnfNext)
    tnfKind = 0
    if tnfNextSize > 0
        tnfShift = (tnfNextSize - CELL_COLUMN_COUNT) / 2
        tnfX = (tnfCell mod CELL_COLUMN_COUNT) + tnfShift
        tnfY = (tnfCell / CELL_COLUMN_COUNT) + tnfShift
        tnfKind = tutorialLayoutKind(tnfNext, tnfX, tnfY)
    else
        ` the kinds are tried in turn, starting from a different one in every cell. a cell only touches
        ` four others, so one of the seven is always free.
        tnfTry = 0
        while tnfTry < 7
            tnfPick = TUTORIAL_KINDS(((tnfCell + tnfTry) mod 7) + 1)
            tnfGroup = countFishGroup(tnfCell, tnfPick, 2)
            if tnfGroup < 2
                tnfKind = tnfPick
                tnfTry = 7
            endif
            tnfTry = tnfTry + 1
        endwhile
        if tnfKind = 0 then tnfKind = TUTORIAL_KINDS(1)
    endif
endfunction tnfKind


` 1 when a swap between these two cells is not allowed on a little board, and the cursor shakes its
` head. any swap is allowed, but none once the board has popped, until the next board is in, so
` that nothing changes under the board as it grows. startLiveMove asks this about every swap.
function tutorialBlocksSwap(tbsA, tbsB)
    tbsBlocked = 0
    if PUZZLE_ON
        if REQUEST_COMBO_CHECK then tbsBlocked = 1 `the swaps wait for the board to settle. see THE RULES in fish_headers_puzzle.
        if PUZZLE_CLEARED_MS > 0 then tbsBlocked = 1
    endif
    if TUTORIAL_BOARD
        if TUTORIAL_STEP_DONE then tbsBlocked = 1
    endif
    if tbsBlocked
        cursorShakeNo()
    endif
endfunction tbsBlocked


` a swap on a little board popped nothing. judgeMultiplierSwaps comes here. the angler talks about what
` is happening on the board. it does not nag about the multiplier. see tutorial_visit.
function tutorialMissed()
    if TUTORIAL_BOARD = 0 then exitfunction
    if TUTORIAL_STEP_DONE then exitfunction
    TUTORIAL_SWAPS = TUTORIAL_SWAPS + 1

    ` the long way home, while it can be seen
    if TUTORIAL_STAGE = 4
        if TUTORIAL_SWAPS = 1
            guideSay(lockey$("intro.ang.turn"))
        endif
        if TUTORIAL_SWAPS = 4
            if tutorialLooksAway()
                guideSay(lockey$("intro.ang.wrong"))
            endif
        endif
    endif
    if TUTORIAL_STAGE = 5
        if TUTORIAL_SWAPS = 3
            guideSay(lockey$("intro.ang.same2"))
        endif
    endif
endfunction


` 1 when a seahorse looks left, which is the one that is being brought home
function tutorialLooksAway()
    tlaIs = 0
    tlaLast = CELL_COUNT - 1
    for tlaI = 0 to tlaLast
        if CELLS(tlaI).value = TUTORIAL_KINDS(6)
            if SCHOOL_FACE(tlaI) < 0 then tlaIs = 1
        endif
    next
endfunction tlaIs


` the main loop comes here on every frame of a little board. if the player has stopped, it says that is
` fine. it does not say so twice on one board.
function tutorialWatch()
    twNow = game ms()
    twAny = new any input()
    if twAny then TUTORIAL_IDLE_MS = twNow
    if TUTORIAL_STEP_DONE then exitfunction
    if TUTORIAL_WAIT_SAID then exitfunction
    if ANGLER_SPEAKING + GUIDE_QUEUED > 0
        TUTORIAL_IDLE_MS = twNow
        exitfunction
    endif
    if twNow - TUTORIAL_IDLE_MS < TUTORIAL_IDLE_LIMIT then exitfunction
    TUTORIAL_WAIT_SAID = 1
    guideSay(lockey$("intro.ang.wait"))
endfunction


` the info key, on a little board. it is coming. and then it stops answering.
function tutorialTooSoon()
    TUTORIAL_INFO_TRIES = TUTORIAL_INFO_TRIES + 1
    if TUTORIAL_INFO_TRIES = 1
        guideSay(lockey$("intro.ang.soon1"))
    endif
    if TUTORIAL_INFO_TRIES = 2
        guideSay(lockey$("intro.ang.soon2"))
    endif
endfunction


` one cell of the board that the game was dealt comes back, and its fish grows in. tutorial_open_sea
` comes here for every cell, and frame_scale_wave is what sizes them.
function tutorialDealCell(tdcCell)
    CELLS(tdcCell).value = TUTORIAL_DEAL(tdcCell)
    SCHOOL_FACE(tdcCell) = TUTORIAL_DEAL_FACE(tdcCell)
    SCHOOL_SHOWN#(tdcCell) = 0
    CELLS(tdcCell).comboForce = 0
    CELLS(tdcCell).comboBlownUp = 0
    clearCellStack(tdcCell)
    GLOW_TURN#(tdcCell) = 0
    RAINBOW_FISH(tdcCell) = 0
    updateCell(CELLS(tdcCell))
    set sprite alpha CELLS(tdcCell).spriteId, 255
    hide sprite CELLS(tdcCell).fxSpriteId
    create basic tween CELLS(tdcCell).scaleWaveTweenId, 0, 1, TUTORIAL_FISH_GROW, 0
    size sprite CELLS(tdcCell).spriteId, 0, 0
    show sprite CELLS(tdcCell).spriteId
endfunction


` the rest of the game goes back to how it was dealt: the streams of the seed, how many fish have come in,
` the moves and the multiplier. a seed plays the same game, with the tutorial or without it.
function tutorialDealDone()
    for tddI = 0 to 399
        SCHOOL_FACE(tddI) = TUTORIAL_DEAL_FACE(tddI)
    next
    SCHOOL_SPAWNS = TUTORIAL_DEAL_SPAWNS
    for tddI = 0 to 2
        set random stream state tddI, TUTORIAL_RNG(tddI * 2), TUTORIAL_RNG(tddI * 2 + 1)
    next
    CURRENT_MOVE_COUNT = 0
    resetMultiplier()
    coralTrailClear()
endfunction


` THE QUESTION MARKS. one more question mark shows up at this spot, and drifts up from it. the angler
` brings them when it says that the sea can end a few ways. they are only for show, so where they go is
` rolled with rnd.
function tutorialMarkSpawn(tmkX#, tmkY#)
    tmkI = TUTORIAL_MARK_NEXT
    TUTORIAL_MARK_NEXT = (TUTORIAL_MARK_NEXT + 1) mod TUTORIAL_MARK_COUNT
    TUTORIAL_MARK_BORN(tmkI) = game ms()
    TUTORIAL_MARK_X#(tmkI) = tmkX#
    TUTORIAL_MARK_Y#(tmkI) = tmkY#
    size text y TUTORIAL_MARK_TEXTS(tmkI), 12 + rnd(3) * 4
    show text TUTORIAL_MARK_TEXTS(tmkI)
endfunction


` move every question mark that is up along: it drifts up, sways, fades in, and fades away at the end
function tutorialMarksStep()
    tmsNow = game ms()
    tmsLife# = TUTORIAL_MARK_LIFE
    for tmsI = 0 to TUTORIAL_MARK_COUNT - 1
        if TUTORIAL_MARK_BORN(tmsI) > 0
            tmsAge# = tmsNow - TUTORIAL_MARK_BORN(tmsI)
            if tmsAge# >= tmsLife#
                TUTORIAL_MARK_BORN(tmsI) = 0
                hide text TUTORIAL_MARK_TEXTS(tmsI)
            else
                tmsT# = tmsAge# / tmsLife#
                tmsAlpha# = 1
                if tmsT# < .2 then tmsAlpha# = tmsT# / .2
                if tmsT# > .6 then tmsAlpha# = (1 - tmsT#) / .4
                tmsX# = TUTORIAL_MARK_X#(tmsI) + sin(tmsAge# * .004 + tmsI) * TUTORIAL_MARK_SWAY
                tmsY# = TUTORIAL_MARK_Y#(tmsI) - tmsT# * TUTORIAL_MARK_RISE
                set text position TUTORIAL_MARK_TEXTS(tmsI), tmsX#, tmsY#
                set text alpha TUTORIAL_MARK_TEXTS(tmsI), 220 * tmsAlpha#
            endif
        endif
    next
endfunction


` put every question mark away
function tutorialMarksClear()
    for tmcI = 0 to TUTORIAL_MARK_COUNT - 1
        TUTORIAL_MARK_BORN(tmcI) = 0
        hide text TUTORIAL_MARK_TEXTS(tmcI)
    next
endfunction
